DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhoossttnnaammee utility prints the name of the current host.  The super-user
     can set the hostname by supplying an argument; this is usually done in
     the initialization script _/_e_t_c_/_r_c_._d_/_h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e, normally run at boot time.
     This script uses the _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e variable in _/_e_t_c_/_r_c_._c_o_n_f.

     Options:

     --ff    Include domain information in the printed name.  This is the de‐
           fault behavior.

     --ss    Trim off any domain information from the printed name.

     --dd    Only print domain information.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Set the host name of the machine and check the result:

           $ hostname beastie.localdomain.org
           $ hostname
           beastie.localdomain.org

     Do not show domain information:

           $ hostname -s
           beastie

     Show only domain information:

           $ hostname -d
           localdomain.org

